From 51c1c0dfee2083c3de6ead5cfb8930b71cbcd929 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:26:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0135: shift the HUD's DISPLAYED position via the pane's local
 (log-44, user direction)

hud_edge no longer reconstructs an absolute original global and writes
(e_orig + tdx) to +0x70. It shifts the pane's LOCAL translation (+0x30)
and LOCAL scale (+0x48) by the effective delta and never writes +0x70:
the game composes it from the local, so the shift reaches the display
through the game's own composition. This needs no stored layout value
(log-44 criterion (c): (263,71) is not in the pane struct), and it fixes
both device failures: a static pane's +0x70 was never composed, so its
e_orig was (0,0) and the write pushed it to -140 off-screen; a dynamic
pane's +0x70 was recomposed after the write, so the compass stayed
visually unmoved. After writing a pane's local the hook marks the pane
itself dirty (flags bit 4) and its descendants dirty, so the game
recomposes +0x70 in the same Calculate call. Edge, manual drag and hide
are all local deltas (hide is a local +10000). Parent compensation is the
child's target minus the parent's applied delta, scale as a ratio; the
old (c) same-transform gate is gone. BINDING v13 -> v14.
---
