+// the delta is relative, so the unknown layout term cancels out. After
+// writing a pane's local, the hook marks the pane itself dirty (flags bit 4
+// at +0x58) and its descendants dirty, so the game recomposes +0x70 from
+// the shifted local in the same Calculate call.
+// A moved pane's original LOCAL is stored in a small table (state +0x300,
 // 96 128-byte entries, sixteen per element -- up to sixteen layout instances can
-// match the same element) and the modified matrix is always re-derived from that
