-// Parent compensation (0123, revised 0130): some matched panes are CHILDREN
-// of other matched panes -- the moon icon (PicIconSh / PicIcon) and its number
-// (TxtTotalShine, when its parent is a Counter) sit inside the moons
-// 'Counter' group, and the hints text (TxtGuide01) sits inside the compass
-// 'PicStrap' strip -- so a child's game-computed global matrix already
-// carries its parent's transform, and applying the child's own transform on
-// top of it would move the child twice. The stored "original" is therefore
-// the UNMODIFIED global matrix: when the hook sees a matched pane whose
-// parent also has a table entry, it undoes the parent's applied transform
-// (dx_m, dy_m, k_m, stored in the parent's entry, about the parent's centre
-// C, computed from the parent's stored original matrix and the parent pane's
-// size/origin) before deriving the child's modified matrix:
-//     g_unmod = S_C(1/k_m) * T(-dx_m,-dy_m) * g,  mod = D_child * g_unmod
-// (exact: a translate, then a scale about C; when the parent's transform is
-// the identity the undo is skipped, so the common case is untouched, and
-// when the parent and the child want the SAME transform -- and the child
-// actually inherited the parent's move -- the two cancel exactly and the
-// child's matrix is left bit-identical). A hidden parent is undone too (its
-// +10000 off-screen push is subtracted as well), so hiding the parent does
-// not hide the child.
-// (0130, 0132) The undo above is exact only for a DYNAMIC child, whose +0x70 was
-// composed by the game and carries its parent's move. A STATIC child's +0x70
-// never carried it, so the subtraction is spurious for it -- but the stored
-// original's translation is then rebuilt from the full parent chain (0132:
-// the sum of the local transforms (+0x30) from the pane up to the root,
-// never any +0x70), which discards the spurious subtraction before it
