+// Parent compensation (0123, revised 0135): a child of a matched parent
+// must not be double-shifted. The old design undid the parent's transform
+// from the child's global matrix (hud_edge_unparent); the local design is
+// simpler: a pane's displayed shift is its parent's applied shift plus its
+// own local shift, so the child's local delta is its own target minus the
+// parent's applied delta (read from the parent's table entry -- a parent
+// with no entry, or a fresh entry, applied the identity, and the parent's
+// Calculate runs before the child's, so its entry is already written when
+// the child is processed). The scale is the ratio: the child's displayed
+// scale is the parent's applied scale times the child's local scale, so the
+// local scale is the target scale divided by the parent's k. A child that
